        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0412" n="1066" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1066"/>

                <head>No. 507.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Schuyler to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 22, 1875</date>.
                        (Received July 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 123.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my last dispatch, No. 122, on
                    the subject of the arrest of the Peruvian bark “<hi rendition="#italic">Maria
                        Luz</hi>,” I have the honor to inclose to you herewith, marked 1 and 2, a
                    copy and translation of the decision of the Emperor of Russia in the matter.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EUGENE SCHUYLER.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d208-a1.xml" xpointer="d208-a1"/>
            </div>
